.TH GETMNTENT_R 3
.SH NAME
getmntent_r \- reentrant read of a filesystem table entry
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <mntent.h>
.PP
.BI "struct mntent *getmntent_r(FILE *" stream ", struct mntent *" mntbuf ,
.BI "char *" buf ", int " buflen ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getmntent_r
is the reentrant equivalent of
.BR getmntent (3).
It reads the next entry from the filesystem-table
.I stream
(opened with
.BR setmntent (3))
and parses it into the caller-supplied
.I mntbuf
structure, whose string members point into the caller-supplied scratch buffer
.I buf
of length
.IR buflen .
Blank lines and
.B #
comments are skipped.
The
.I mnt_freq
and
.I mnt_passno
fields default to 0 when absent.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.I mntbuf
on success, or NULL at end of file or on a usage error (NULL argument or
non-positive
.IR buflen ).
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS 4
.EX
FILE *fp = setmntent("/etc/fstab", "r");
struct mntent ent;
char buf[1024];
while (getmntent_r(fp, &ent, buf, sizeof buf))
    printf("%s on %s type %s\\n",
           ent.mnt_fsname, ent.mnt_dir, ent.mnt_type);
endmntent(fp);
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getmntent (3),
.BR setmntent (3),
.BR fstab (5)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
